+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
+**Purpose**: The store connection, the argument-parsing shell with its reserved exit statuses, the module entry point, and the test fixtures — everything every user story needs before it can add a single command
+
+**⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete
+
+- [ ] T004 Implement `connect(path)` in `src/bookmarks/storage.py`: open the SQLite file with `sqlite3.connect`, set `row_factory = sqlite3.Row`, and apply the schema idempotently with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bookmarks (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, url TEXT NOT NULL, title TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', tags TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '')` — `AUTOINCREMENT` is required so ids are never reused (FR-003, FR-008, research.md D1/D2); no indexes, no `UNIQUE` on `url` (duplicates are allowed), no module-level cached connection (constitution: no hidden state)
+- [ ] T005 Implement the usage-error parser class in `src/bookmarks/cli.py`: a three-line `argparse.ArgumentParser` subclass overriding `error(message)` to write the message to `sys.stderr` and `raise SystemExit(1)`, so argparse's default status 2 cannot collide with the reserved FR-009 meaning (research.md D5; contracts/cli.md exit-status table)
+- [ ] T006 Implement `build_parser()` in `src/bookmarks/cli.py` using the T005 subclass: the global option `--db PATH` defaulting to `bookmarks.db` in the current working directory and preceding `COMMAND` (FR-002), plus a required subparser group into which each user story registers its own command (FR-001)
+- [ ] T007 Implement `main(argv=None)` in `src/bookmarks/cli.py` (depends on T004, T005, T006): call `sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding="utf-8")` and the same for `sys.stderr` before any output (research.md D7), parse arguments, dispatch to the selected handler, and return its integer status; catch only `sqlite3.Error` and `OSError` raised while opening or using the store, re-report them as a stderr diagnostic naming the `--db` path and the underlying error, and return 1 (FR-006; no bare `except`, no `except Exception: pass`, per Principle II)
+- [ ] T008 [P] Create `src/bookmarks/__main__.py` containing only the import of `main` and `raise SystemExit(main())`, so `python -m bookmarks` works (FR-001) while importing the package during tests executes nothing
+- [ ] T009 [P] Create `tests/conftest.py` with three fixtures: a store path under pytest's `tmp_path`, an in-process runner calling `cli.main(argv)` and capturing streams via `capsys`, and a subprocess runner invoking `[sys.executable, "-m", "bookmarks", *args]` with `env={"PYTHONPATH": "src"}` that returns `(returncode, stdout, stderr)` so real exit statuses and stream separation are observable (research.md D9)
+
+**Checkpoint**: Foundation ready — `python -m bookmarks --help` works, the store opens, and user story implementation can begin
