+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Capture a link and see it again later (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: `add URL [--title TITLE] [--tags TAGS]` stores a bookmark and prints its id; `list` prints every stored bookmark as tab-separated fields in ascending id order; the store is created on first use and survives across invocations; a bad URL is rejected with status 2 and changes nothing.
+
+**Independent Test**: Add two bookmarks in one invocation each against a fresh `--db` path, then run `list` in a separate invocation and confirm both appear in ascending id order with the ids that were printed on add — `1<TAB>https://docs.python.org<TAB>Python docs<TAB>docs,python` and `2<TAB>https://example.com<TAB><TAB>`. Then add `ftp://example.com` and confirm status 2, an empty stdout, a stderr diagnostic, and a byte-identical listing.
+
+### Tests for User Story 1
+
+> **NOTE: Write these tests FIRST and confirm they FAIL before implementing T016–T022**
+
+- [ ] T010 [P] [US1] Write `tests/test_add.py` covering FR-007 (stdout is exactly the decimal id and a newline, nothing else), FR-008 (first bookmark in a store gets id `1`, each subsequent id strictly increases), FR-010 (an omitted `--title` lists as an empty field), FR-011 (input `"  python , , cli, python "` stores and displays as `cli,python`; `--tags ","` and an omitted `--tags` both yield an empty tags field), and the FR-009 error path (`ftp://example.com`, a bare domain, an empty string and `HTTP://example.com` each give status 2, a stderr diagnostic naming the URL and the expected `http://`/`https://` prefixes, empty stdout, and — against a not-yet-existing `--db` path — no store file created at all). Each test names its requirement in its name or docstring (Principle III)
+- [ ] T011 [P] [US1] Write `tests/test_cli.py` covering FR-002 (`--db PATH` is used as the store; with `--db` omitted the store is `bookmarks.db` in the current working directory, verified with `monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)`), FR-003 (the first command against a non-existent path succeeds with no initialisation step and the file then exists), FR-004 (`add` in one subprocess then `list` in another against the same path returns the bookmark), FR-005 (status 0 on each success path), and FR-006 (a rejected command writes to stderr, writes nothing to stdout, exits non-zero, and leaves the listing identical to the listing taken before it — SC-007)
+- [ ] T012 [P] [US1] Write `tests/test_list_search.py` covering FR-012 (`list` prints every bookmark in ascending id order), FR-015 (exactly four tab-separated fields in the order id, URL, title, tags; a bookmark with neither title nor tags yields two trailing empty fields so the line ends with two tabs; no quoting or escaping is applied) and FR-016 for `list` (an empty store prints nothing at all — not a blank line — and exits 0)
+- [ ] T013 [US1] Add the FR-023 fidelity cases to `tests/test_add.py` (same file as T010, so not parallel with it): a non-ASCII URL, title and tags (for example `https://例え.jp`, `日本語のページ — notes`, `日本語,ドキュメント`) are stored and reproduced character-for-character in the `list` output, with no case folding and no trimming beyond the FR-011 tag trimming, under a `C`/`POSIX` locale as well
+
