+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Find the link you half-remember (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: `search TEXT` prints every bookmark whose title or URL contains TEXT as a substring ignoring letter case; `list --tag TAG` prints only bookmarks carrying TAG as a whole tag, matched exactly and case-sensitively. Both use the same per-line format as `list`.
+
+**Independent Test**: With bookmark 1 titled `Python docs` at `https://docs.python.org` tagged `docs,python` and bookmark 2 at `https://example.com` untagged, confirm `search PYTHON` prints only line 1, `search EXAMPLE` prints only line 2 (matched in its URL), `list --tag docs` prints only line 1, and `list --tag doc` prints nothing with status 0.
+
+### Tests for User Story 2
+
+> **NOTE: Write these tests FIRST and confirm they FAIL before implementing T024–T027**
+
+- [ ] T023 [US2] Extend `tests/test_list_search.py` (the file created in T012) with FR-013 coverage (`--tag docs` matches a bookmark tagged `docs,python`; `--tag doc` matches nothing because the match is on a whole tag, not a substring; `--tag Python` does not match the tag `python` because tag matching is case-sensitive; a bookmark with no tags is never matched) and FR-014 coverage (`PYTHON` matches the title `Python docs`; a substring present only in the URL matches; a search whose casing differs from the stored text still matches; `TEXT` is matched literally, so `%` and `_` are not wildcards), both asserting ascending id order, and FR-016 for `search` (no matches → no output, status 0)
+
+### Implementation for User Story 2
