+- [ ] T025 [P] [US2] Implement `matches_text(row, needle)` in `src/bookmarks/cli.py`: `needle.casefold() in row["title"].casefold() or needle.casefold() in row["url"].casefold()`, using `str.casefold` so there are no wildcard metacharacters and folding covers Unicode rather than ASCII only (FR-014, research.md D3)
+- [ ] T026 [US2] Add the optional `--tag TAG` argument to the `list` subparser in `src/bookmarks/cli.py` and filter the rows from `list_bookmarks` through `matches_tag` in the `list` handler when it is supplied, preserving ascending id order and the status-0-on-no-match behaviour (FR-013, FR-016; depends on T022, T024)
+- [ ] T027 [US2] Register the `search` subparser (positional `TEXT`, required) and implement its handler in `src/bookmarks/cli.py`, reusing `list_bookmarks`, `matches_text` and `format_bookmark_line`, printing matches in ascending id order and returning 0 including when nothing matches (FR-014, FR-015, FR-016; depends on T015, T018, T025)
