+- [ ] T032 [P] [US4] Implement `export_csv(rows, stream)` in `src/bookmarks/cli.py` using `csv.writer(stream, lineterminator="\n")`: write the header row `id,url,title,tags` then one row per bookmark with the stored comma-joined tags string, relying on the writer's standard quoting for values containing the delimiter, quotes or line breaks (FR-019, FR-022, research.md D6, contracts/output-formats.md)
+- [ ] T033 [P] [US4] Implement `export_json(rows, stream)` in `src/bookmarks/cli.py` using `json.dump(..., ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)` followed by a trailing newline: a single array of objects with `id` as a number, `url` and `title` as strings, and `tags` as the alphabetical array obtained by splitting the stored string (`[]` when it is empty); an empty store yields `[]` (FR-020, FR-022, research.md D6)
