+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: no dependencies — start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: depends on Setup — **blocks all user stories**
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: depends on Foundational only
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: depends on Foundational; extends the `list` handler (T022) and the test file (T012) that User Story 1 creates
+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: depends on Foundational only — its own storage function, subparser, handler and test file
+- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: depends on Foundational and on `list_bookmarks` (T015) from User Story 1
+- **Polish (Phase 7)**: depends on all four stories being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: no dependencies on other stories. Fully independent, and the MVP.
+- **US2 (P2)**: independently testable, but shares two files with US1 — `src/bookmarks/cli.py`'s `list` handler (adds `--tag`) and `tests/test_list_search.py` (appends the search and tag-filter tests). This is the only cross-story file overlap in the plan and follows from plan.md's fixed test-module layout; sequence US1 before US2 rather than running them in parallel on the same files.
+- **US3 (P3)**: independently testable. Touches `storage.py` and `cli.py` but adds only new functions and a new subparser, and its own `tests/test_delete.py`.
+- **US4 (P4)**: independently testable. Reuses `list_bookmarks` read-only; adds only new functions, a new subparser and its own `tests/test_export.py`.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written first and must FAIL before the implementation tasks in that phase
+- `storage.py` query functions before the `cli.py` handlers that call them
+- Pure helpers (`normalise_tags`, `validate_url`, `format_bookmark_line`, `matches_tag`, `matches_text`, `export_csv`, `export_json`) before the handlers that compose them
+- Subparser registration before the handler that consumes its arguments
+- Story complete and its checkpoint validated before moving to the next priority
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- Setup: T002 and T003 run in parallel after T001
+- Foundational: T008 and T009 run in parallel with each other and with T004–T007 once T005/T006 exist in signature form; T004 (storage) is independent of T005/T006 (parser)
+- US1: the three test modules T010, T011, T012 in parallel (different files); T013 follows T010 because it appends to the same file; helpers T016, T017, T018 in parallel (different functions, no shared state)
+- US2: T024 and T025 in parallel
+- US4: T032 and T033 in parallel
+- Polish: T035–T038 in parallel; T039–T041 are sequential validation runs
+- Across stories, once Foundational is done: US3 and US4 can proceed in parallel with each other; US2 should follow US1 because of the shared `list` handler and test file
+
